{#
ComponentMetadataRule fixture — page template OK case.

Page templates (those whose path contains `/templates/page/`) follow a different
metadata convention: name / usage / description / weight — NO mandatory `category`.
This fixture verifies that omitting `category` on a page template does NOT trigger
a warning.

The file lives under `fixtures/templates/page/` precisely so the rule's
page-template detection (`str_contains($path, '/templates/page/')`) fires — the
exemption is what's under test, so the path has to satisfy it. The default
config.php Finder only scans `static/templates/`, so this fixture is NOT linted
automatically; lint it explicitly to exercise the exemption:

vendor/bin/twig-cs-fixer lint --config tests/config/twig-wordpress.php tests/Fixtures/Twig/templates/page/component-metadata-page-ok-fixture.twig

Expected: 0 warnings, 0 errors (ComponentMetadata) — no `category` required for page templates

See: component-metadata-ok-fixture.twig (component with full metadata)
component-metadata-fail-fixture.twig (component with multiple violations)

